Phase 1: Push Your Code to GitHub
Both Render and Vercel work by connecting to your GitHub account. Every time you push an update to GitHub, they will automatically update your live website!

Go to GitHub.com and create two new repositories:

Name one splitwise-backend

Name the other splitwise-frontend

Open your terminal, navigate to your backend folder (debt-simplifier), and push your code to the backend repo.

Open a second terminal, navigate to your frontend folder, and push your React code to the frontend repo.
(If you need help with the Git commands to do this, let me know!)


Phase 2: Deploy the Backend (Render)
You must deploy the backend first, because your frontend needs to know its new live URL.

Go to Render.com and sign up with your GitHub account.

Click New + and select Web Service.

Connect your splitwise-backend repository.

Fill in the details:

Name: splitwise-api

Environment: Node

Build Command: npm install

Start Command: node server.js

Instance Type: Free

CRITICAL STEP: Scroll down to Environment Variables. Add a variable named MONGO_URI and paste your exact MongoDB Atlas connection string as the value.

Click Create Web Service.

Wait a few minutes. Render will give you a live URL that looks something like https://splitwise-api-xyz.onrender.com. Copy this URL!




Phase 3: Connect Frontend to the Live Backend
Right now, your React app is hardcoded to look for http://localhost:3000. If you deploy it like this, it will break!

Open your code editor and go to frontend/src/App.jsx.

Near the top (around line 5), find this line:

JavaScript
const API = 'http://localhost:3000/api';
Change it to your new Render URL:

JavaScript
const API = 'https://splitwise-api-xyz.onrender.com/api'; // Use YOUR exact Render link!
Save the file, and push this update to your splitwise-frontend GitHub repository.

Phase 4: Deploy the Frontend (Vercel)
This is the easiest part. Vercel is absolute magic.

Go to Vercel.com and log in with GitHub.

Click Add New -> Project.

You will see a list of your GitHub repos. Click Import next to your splitwise-frontend repository.

Vercel will auto-detect that it is a Vite/React app. You don't need to change any settings!

Click Deploy.

Vercel will build your app in about 30 seconds, do a little confetti animation, and give you a beautiful live .vercel.app domain.
